  (text "FROM THE HAND-WRITTEN NETLIST THIS SHEET REPLACES (verbatim; the part notes are on each part's Note field):\n\nAUTHORITATIVE for connectivity. THE DRAWING IS ON ANOTHER PAGE - carrier.md §2, which draws the reference, the\nbuffer, the sensor and the ADC in one picture because they are one signal path. This circuit owns the\nreference and both halves of the OPA2197; carrier/breath-adc and interfaces/breath-sense-link own the rest and\nnetlist it against the same drawing.\n\nTHE REFERENCE'S INPUT IS PROTECTED, AND THE TVS ON THE RAIL DOES NOT DO IT. The REF5050's input is 18 V\nabsolute maximum [ds REF5050.pdf p.5], and the rail's SMAJ15A only starts to break down at 16.7-18.5 V and\nclamps at 24.4 V [ds LITTELFUSE-SMAJ-SERIES-SMAJ15A.pdf p.2]. So the reference has its own: R-REF-IN in\nseries, D-REF-CLAMP to the star behind it. 1.2 mA at most [ds p.8] drops 0.4 V; at the SMAJ's clamp the zener\ntakes (24.4 - 15.75) / 330 = 26 mA, and holds the input under 18 V for the 10/1000 us surge the SMAJ is rated\nat - an RC alone would not, its time constant being shorter.\n\nONE PACKAGE, TWO JOBS: half A buffers the 5.000 V into the sensor, half B the sensor's output before anything\nloads it. Single supply from +12 V, V- on the analog star.\n\nThe REF5050's other pins [ds datasheets/analog/REF5050.pdf Table 5-1]: TEMP, TRIM/NR and NC are left open -\nthe trim and the noise-reduction capacitor are not used; DNC must not be connected." (at 256.54 38.099999999999994 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 0f044db4-4ac3-511b-98ad-fcf4fe25b8dd))
